---
import StudyLayout from "../../../layouts/StudyLayout.astro";

const results = [
  [
    "One subject",
    "Pass",
    "One initial set of stellar encounters, comparing appearance and behaviour through the pilot decisions they create. The open ship-motion study owns changes to handling, which this opening holds fixed; no open study owns the stellar answer.",
  ],
  [
    "Grounded",
    "Pass with findings",
    "The fixed Sun baseline matches its specification and implementation: collection, gravitational pull, exposure and lethal contact. The earlier study distinguishes the stated stellar properties, and the open families, behaviour and cues can be compared in built flight examples. Comparison conditions needed clarification.",
  ],
  [
    "Consequence",
    "Pass",
    "The game gains a small initial set of additional stellar encounter identities whose readable opportunities and dangers change how a pilot approaches, collects and escapes. Travel and progression are outside this cycle.",
  ],
] as const;
---

<StudyLayout>
  <section>
    <h2>Stellar encounters — question review of 01</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/lab/studies/stellar-encounters-2026-11-11"
        >Return to the study</a
      >
    </p>
    <p>
      Historical review: this study was subsequently stopped on 11 November 2026
      after the designer assessed it as failing the intended breadth of stellar
      identity. The results below concern the original opening, not the
      rewritten closure record, and do not establish design success.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tested on 11 November 2026 by a clean-context, read-only reviewer with no
      part in framing and no expected outcome. This tests whether the question
      can be answered, not design quality or gameplay success. The opening was
      corrected after the review and has not been retested.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Metric</th>
          <th>Result</th>
          <th>Reason</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {results.map(([metric, result, reason]) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{metric}</th>
            <td>{result}</td>
            <td>{reason}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <h2>Findings and responses</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>1 / Comparison controls were incomplete.</strong>
      “Same ship and starting resources” left fitting and flight mode implicit.
      Hull and fitting determine handling, collection and capacity; practice
      suppresses applied exposure and death. Corrected in 01: retain the same
      fitting and resource protection rules as well. This was an omission, not a
      false claim or failed metric.
    </p>
    <p>
      Evidence: <code>docs/specs/game/ships/spec.md:40–45,73–82</code>;
      <code>docs/specs/game/world/star/spec.md:57</code>;
      <code>packages/mode-a/src/lib/simulation.ts:474,497</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>2 / The handling baseline needs a reproducible snapshot.</strong>
      “Current ship handling” is specified, but the related motion study remains
      open. The eventual comparison evidence must name its production
      build/configuration. Retained as an evidence requirement for exploration;
      no change to the opening’s scope is needed, and the open motion study is
      not a dependency.
    </p>
    <p>
      Evidence: <code>docs/specs/game/ships/spec.md:62–72</code>; the
      ship-motion entry in <code>apps/web/src/data/studies.ts</code>.
    </p>
    <h2>Grounding evidence</h2>
    <p>
      Standard-Sun intent and mechanics:
      <code>docs/specs/game/world/star/spec.md:5–6,19–28</code>; collection,
      exposure and contact:
      <code>packages/core/src/lib/physics/Physics.ts:277–298,310–325</code>;
      production Sun and death handling:
      <code>packages/mode-a/src/lib/simulation.ts:123,381–383</code>. Stellar
      dimensions:
      <a href="/lab/studies/suns-2026-11-07#stellar-model"
        >earlier Sun study, 02.1</a
      >. The registry and study contract were also inspected for ownership and
      cycle-zero authority. Historical proposals were not treated as production
      contracts.
    </p>
    <h2>Not checked by the reviewer</h2>
    <p>
      Rendered layout, keyboard operation, builds, automated tests, gameplay
      outcomes, design quality and external astrophysical accuracy. No new
      encounter examples existed to inspect. The astrophysics wording was
      checked against the referenced repository study; scientific research and
      concrete encounter comparisons remain exploration work.
    </p>
  </section>
</StudyLayout>

<style>
table {
  width: 100%;
  border-collapse: collapse;
  margin-block: var(--spacing-lg);
}
th,
td {
  padding: var(--spacing-sm);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  text-align: left;
  vertical-align: top;
}
code {
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}
</style>
